    2. For each pair, choose a dot-grid size (2-8 rows x 2-5 cols).
    3. Place dot-grid origins so at least one pair of expanded bboxes overlaps,
       all fit within 20x20, and no expanded bbox covers legend cells (rows 0..N-1, cols 0-1).
    4. For overlapping pairs, remove dots of the lower-priority object at grid positions
       inside the higher-priority object's expanded bbox.
    5. Write legend to rows 0..N-1 cols 0-1; write remaining dots onto bg grid.
    6. Verify via solver that output is non-trivial (overlapping fills visible).
