0019:     - One color appears only as four pixels on the grid boundary.
0020:     - Those boundary pixels mark the rows or columns of the output lines.
0021: 
0022:     Rule:
0023:     - Find the color whose pixels all lie on the boundary.
0024:     - For markers on the top or bottom edge, draw a full vertical line through that column.
0025:     - For markers on the left or right edge, draw a full horizontal line through that row.
0026: 
0027:     Key insight:
0028:     - Boundary-only pixels are line endpoints; all other scattered colors are noise.
0029:     """
0030:     # Find the used color
0031:     all_color = np.unique(input_grid)
0032: 
0033:     # Find the color all on the boundary, which is the lines' color
0034:     def on_boundary(rr, cc):
0035:         return (
0036:             rr == 0
0037:             or rr == input_grid.shape[0] - 1
0038:             or cc == 0
0039:             or cc == input_grid.shape[1] - 1
0040:         )
0041:     
0042:     # Get the color all on the boundary, which is the lines' color
